      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] On ARM Cortex-M, the Link Register (`lr`) is not stripped (it uses `M` instead of `M_GPR`). Since the RISC-V Return Address (`ra`) serves the same purpose—holding a code pointer which is vital for debugging and generally doesn\u0027t contain sensitive data—consider leaving it unstripped by using `M(ra, riscv.regs[29], ra)` here.\n\nIf you make this change, you will also need to update the test in `zephyr/test/hwtest/src/panic.c` so that it doesn\u0027t expect `ra` to be `0` when `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_PANIC_STRIP_GPR` is enabled (e.g. by removing `ra` from `expected_regs` or skipping it in the verification loop).",
